      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I don't think they're referring to jumping using the in-game buttons, but rather jumping in real life with a VR Headset. As of now, jumping with just a vr headset causes your real head to go higher than your virtual head, as your virtual body does not leave the ground. Likewise when using playspace mover to pull yourself up, it pulls you out of your body.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
